WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.584 --> 00:00:04.421
Dad! Do something about Soichi!

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.715
Easier said than done.

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:10.051
He's a completely lost cause.

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:12.887
What? Then I'm moving out!

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:14.806
No, wait, Koichi!

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.182
I have an idea.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:20.311
I know a carpenter.
I'll have him soundproof your room.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:21.354
How about that?

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:22.480
I guess.

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:29.237
I'm home.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.990
-Oh, Koichi.
-The carpenter's here already?

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.450
That's right.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.327
Your father had him come right away.

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:37.871
Really?

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.546
Mr. Tagaisu, I made some tea.
Please take a break.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:48.965
Hey!

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.675
Hello there!

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.886
My, oh my.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:55.263
Mr. Tagaisu, thank you for coming.

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:58.099
So this must be your eldest son.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.226
Leave it to me.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:04.481
I'll use the latest techniques
to make your room perfectly soundproof.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.357
The latest techniques?

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:07.484
That's right.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:11.780
I'll use four-wall construction
to block external noise.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:14.074
Four walls? That's really something.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.993
There's a reason I chose the number four.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:21.164
The Japanese pronunciation
of the number four means "death."

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.500
Two or three-wall construction won't do.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.295
It only sounds like death
once you have four walls.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:28.505
Right…

